<title>BELGIUM: KEMIRA OY SETS 2 BLN BFR CP PROGRAMME.</title>
<headline>KEMIRA OY SETS 2 BLN BFR CP PROGRAMME.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish chemicals group Kemira Oy will issue up to two billion Belgian francs equivalent ($57 million) of commercial paper, co-lead managers Generale Bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The issue by Kemira Oy and its Dutch Kemira International Finance BV arm will take the form of dematerialised treasury notes in Belgian francs or any other OECD currency.</p>
<p>The programme replaces a similar promissory notes issue dating from 1990, which was the first launched on the Belgian market, Generale Bank said.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
